You may quote excerpts of the book's original prose, free of charge, in
any medium, including in commercial publications. Each time you publish
or share an excerpt under this license, keep its attribution with it.
This condition applies to subsequent sharing of the excerpt as well.

Identify the book by title, name the chapter or section, and include a
link to the source or a bibliographic reference suitable for the medium.
Retain any author, translator, or other source credit supplied for the
quoted passage. A nearby caption, footnote, or spoken credit is sufficient
if the reader or listener can tell which passage it credits.

